// CLAIM: spec 10 constraint — a module-scope `assert` takes a CONSTANT expression, and the definition
// CLAIM: is a closed list, so an element of a constant table is not one even though it is fixed at
// CLAIM: translation time. The constraint used to give the reason as "a value that exists only at run
// CLAIM: time", which is false for a constant table; the refusal is about the list, not about time.
// EXPECT: [E133]
TABLE u8[3] = [1, 2, 3]
assert TABLE[0] == 1
func main() i32 { return 0 }
